y for Ophthalmology: Coming of Age? Asia-Pacific journal of ophthalmology (Philadelphia, Pa). 2021;10: 343–347. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ]; Overview of blockchain technology, specifically as it applies to ophthalmology. 29. Yang Q, Liu Y, Chen T, Tong Y. Federated machine learning: Concept and applications. ACM Transactions on Intelligent Systems and Technology. 2019;10. doi: 10.1145/3298981 [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 30.*. Rieke N, Hancox J, Li W, Milletarì F, Roth HR, Albarqouni S, et al. The future of digital health with federated learning. npj Digital Medicine. 2020;3: 1–7. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ]; Overview of federated learning in healthcare, discussing background, rationale, impact and technical considerations. 31. Mehta N, Lee CS, Mendonça LSM, Raza K, Braun PX, Duker JS, et al. Model-to-Data Approach for Deep Learning in Optical Coherence Tomography Intraretinal Fluid Segmentation. JAMA Ophthalmol. 2020;138: 1017–1024. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 32. Lo J, Yu TT, Ma D, Zang P, Owen JP, Zhang Q, et al. Federated Learning for Microvasculature Segmentation and Diabetic Retinopathy Classification of OCT Data. Ophthalmology Science. 2021;1: 100069. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 33.*. Raghunathan TE. Synthetic data. Annual Review of Statistics and Its Application. 2021;8: 129–140. [ Google Scholar ]; Provides a useful overview of synthetic data, as well as data privacy in general. 34. Goncalves A, Ray P, Soper B, Stevens J, Coyle L, Sales AP. Generation and evaluation of synthetic patient data. BMC Med Res Methodol. 2020;20: 1–40. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Baowaly MK, Lin CC, Liu CL, Chen KT. Synthesizing electronic health records using improved generative adversarial networks. J Am Med Inform Assoc. 2019;26: 228–241. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 36. Kaur D, Sobiesk M, Patil S, Liu J, Bhagat P,