9) [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 52. Marx M, Mosnier I, Venail F, et al. Cochlear implantation and other treatments in single-sided deafness and asymmetric hearing loss: results of a national multicenter study including a randomized controlled trial. Audiol Neurootol. 2021;26(6):414 424. ( 10.1159/000514085) [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 53. Távora-Vieira D, Rajan GP, Van de Heyning P, Mertens G. Evaluating the long-term hearing outcomes of cochlear implant users with single-sided deafness. Otol Neurotol. 2019;40(6):e575 e580. ( 10.1097/MAO.0000000000002235) [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 54. Bagatto M, DesGeorges J, King A, et al. Consensus practice parameter: audiological assessment and management of unilateral hearing loss in children. Int J Audiol. 2019;58(12):805 815. ( 10.1080/14992027.2019.1654620) [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 55. Ellsperman SE, Zwolan TA, Telian SA. Rehabilitation for unilateral deafness–Narrative review comparing a novel bone conduction solution with existing options. Am J Otolaryngol. 2021;42(6):103060. ( 10.1016/j.amjoto.2021.103060) [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 56. Dhanasingh A, Hochmair I. CI in single-sided deafness. Acta Oto-Laryngol. 2021;141(sup1):82 105. ( 10.1080/00016489.2021.1888496) [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 57. Lipschitz N, Kohlberg GD, Scott M, Smith MM, Greinwald JH. Socioeconomic disparities in pediatric single-sided deafness. Otolaryngol Head Neck Surg. 2020;163(4):829 834. ( 10.1177/0194599820923634) [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 58. Seebacher J, Muigg F, Kühn H, et al. Cost-utility analysis of cochlear implantation in adults with single-sided deafness: Austrian and German perspective. Otol Neurotol. 2021;42(6):799 805. ( 10.1097/MAO.0000000000003103) [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 59. Dreyfuss M, Giat Y, Veraguth D, Röösli C, Huber AM, Laske RD. Cost effectiveness of cochlear implantation in single-sided deafness